0..74 Comment "//! Two distinct terms of a theory with a commutative operation are apart."
75..78 Comment "//!"
79..156 Comment "//! A decoder with no arm for an impossible case needs two distinct constants"
157..234 Comment "//! to be apart. A theory that states a commutative meet must keep that fact."
235..308 Comment "//! The two orders of one meet are one term, so no case tells them apart."
309..312 Comment "//!"
313..389 Comment "//! The rules of the theory converge on classes of terms under the symmetry."
390..466 Comment "//! Two closed terms are apart where each pairing of the arguments of a meet"
467..539 Comment "//! finds two distinct operations. The kernel makes this decision again."
540..543 Comment "//!"
544..560 Comment "//! - see: #8323"
